{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Handoff state. Plan CERTIFIED and ticket claimed. A subagent is implementing it in its OWN isolated worktree, branched from origin/main so it lands as an INDEPENDENT change rather than stacking on the six-change stack (which is currently Verified -1).\n\nThe plan was corrected once before certifying, and the correction matters: a module-scope `from rebar.config import LAYER_ORDER` would CYCLE, because config.py:99-101 imports FROM rebar._operation_config, which is the leaf. The shipped approach is a functools.cache accessor with a deferred import, following the precedent already in that module at :199-200."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788398802625402001,"uuid":"f492be91-e4d0-4722-8a0c-5199aed9d2be"}